[ 2.500740] === ITEM 4: WHO WRITES IT ===
[ 2.500741]   PRIMARY = the polling loop: the GPU timestamp inside the report, the landed
[ 2.500743]   payload vs the declared one, and the ordering against GP_GET.
[ 2.500744]   The write-breakpoint is a NEGATIVE CONTROL ONLY. A GPU release is a DMA
[ 2.500746]   write: it never touches the CPU MMU and x86 debug registers watch CPU
[ 2.500747]   accesses only, so SILENCE IS EXPECTED FOR ANY DMA AND PROVES NOTHING.
[ 2.500749]   If it FIRES, a CPU store did it and GPU authorship is REFUTED.
[ 2.500750]   GP_PUT carries the same breakpoint as the KNOWN-POSITIVE that the
[ 2.500752]   mechanism is live -- a census zero needs one.
